('island-echoes-health', 'Island Echoes Health', 2026, 'Full-stack', 'Freelance', true, 3, array['Next.js','Expo','React Native','Express','Supabase']::text[], 'A medical platform that connects patients with clinicians, on web and mobile.', array[]::text[], '', 'https://github.com/Dimmsum/island-echoes-health', 'Island Echoes Health connects patients with clinicians. It''s a freelance build, with a web app and a mobile app sharing one backend.

## How it''s built

- **API:** Express and TypeScript. All business logic lives here.
- **Web:** Next.js App Router.
- **Mobile:** Expo and React Native.
- **Data and auth:** Supabase (PostgreSQL). Every request is checked by the API, with row-level security on every table as a second layer.

More details coming soon.', true),
('root-iq', 'Root IQ', 2026, 'Backend', 'Sagicor Innovation Lab', true, 2, array['.NET','Docker','AWS EC2','GitHub Actions','SQL']::text[], 'Backend work on the Sagicor Innovation Lab''s agricultural management platform.', array[]::text[], '', '', 'Root IQ is an agricultural management platform built at the Sagicor Innovation Lab, a partnership between Sagicor and the University of Technology, Jamaica. My work there is on the backend.

## What I did

- **API:** backend development on the Root IQ .NET API.
- **CI/CD:** set up GitHub Actions pipelines for three environments (dev, UAT and production), deploying Docker containers to AWS EC2.
- **Database docs:** documented 120+ stored procedures across 21 categories, in a format that''s quick for developers and AI tools to search.', true),
('rootyou', 'RootYou', 2026, 'AI', 'In progress', true, 1, array['macOS','Tauri v2','TypeScript','Node.js','Claude','MCP']::text[], 'A desktop AI buddy for macOS. Press a hotkey, ask out loud, and it briefs you from your email, calendar, meetings and code.', array[]::text[], '', '', 'RootYou is an animated buddy that lives on your Mac. Hold a hotkey, ask a question, and it answers from your own streams: Gmail, Google Calendar, Drive and Docs, Granola meeting notes, GitHub and Vercel, plus general chat and web search.

It can also act for you. Ask it to book or move a meeting and it shows a confirm card first, then does it.

## How it''s built

- **Desktop shell:** Tauri v2 with a shared web UI, macOS first.
- **Backend:** hosted TypeScript/Node service, so future Windows and mobile clients reuse it.
- **Connectors:** each data source plugs in through an MCP server.
- **AI:** Anthropic''s Claude.
- **Auth:** Clerk.
- **Character:** its own pixel-sprite design system with 8 base models, 16 faces and 6 palettes. The buddy wanders the screen and can be dragged and poked.

Built solo, test-first, as a product for my own software company.', true),
